# Commercial S7 live discovery refresh

- Prepared at: 2026-08-30T11:21:00Z
- Scope: public SFW HEAD and origin-level crawler discovery only
- Existing public GET runtime: healthy and intentionally left running until the
  versioned live backup, refresh and rollback controls pass review

## Finding

External launch verification found two narrow HTTP quality gaps:

1. the application returned 404 to HEAD on otherwise healthy public GET
   resources;
2. `/robots.txt` and `/sitemap.xml` fell through to the legacy SPA document.

No waitlist, health, legal-page, analytics or security-header failure was found.

## Versioned resolution

- bind the application to merge `935518614d4e9e6ce302c75bf81d6e5ca2a4f1d4`
  and tree `29679c2029d40eefce7dbd3857c5cf4e1f129013`;
- serve explicit host-root robots and sitemap documents from Nginx;
- exclude the Adult Publishing URLs from the disabled/kill-switch sitemap;
- require a new root-owned live backup while the current S7 service is healthy;
- allow refresh only from the exact current release and Nginx hash;
- execute release installation in a subshell so every partial release failure
  enters the bounded rollback handler;
- on failure, restore the exact previous release, editable installation and both
  Nginx files before attempting to restore the prior public service.

## Product boundary

This refresh does not enable Telegram, X, Reddit, AVS, payments, Adult media,
creator submissions, scheduling or publishing. It does not modify the database
schema or public product contract.

## Rollback

The live backup contains both Git bundles, database dump, installed Nginx files,
S7 configuration/unit archives, service state and a strict SHA-256 index. The
controller additionally pins the only accepted rollback source to the current
application SHA/tree and prior installed Nginx SHA.
